name issue_5_bitrate_adjuster
describe libwebrtc's EncoderBitrateAdjuster on (issue #5, PR 2): keyframe bursts every 2 s on a 1.5 Mbps link stay paced out without freezes or a queue
duration 30s
seed 3
bitrate_adjuster on
keyframe_interval 2s
# The port is behind `bitrate_adjuster on` until it is judged against libwebrtc as a whole (#5).
# The expectations lock in the level reached with it on (seed 3, 5 seeds: queue max <= 120 ms,
# e2e p95 <= 200 ms, no freeze); `off` gives queue max 51 ms and e2e p95 109 ms on seed 3.
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=400ms
expect video.freeze_total_ms == 0
expect cc.queue_max_ms < 200
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 250
expect video.avg_kbps > 600
